## 4. Two-Tier Navigation Hierarchy (Outer Launcher vs. Inner Instrument Modes)

Antigravity 2 must maintain a strict separation between **outer product switching** and **inner instrument sub-modes**:

| Layer | Component | Purpose | Audio Engine Behavior on Switch |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Tier 1 (Outer)** | `App.tsx` (`36px` top bar) | Switches between standalone products: **`GROOVEBOX`** $\leftrightarrow$ **`AETHER-8`** (and future instruments). | **Hard Teardown:** Stops clocks, closes outgoing `AudioContext`, unmounts outgoing DOM tree. |
| **Tier 2 (Inner — Groovebox)** | `GrooveboxRoot.tsx` header | Switches Groovebox's internal workflow between **`PLAY` Mode** (live performance) and **`STUDIO` Mode** (deep sound design & sequencing). | **Zero Interruption:** Keeps Groovebox's `AudioContext`, active sequence, and audio playback running seamlessly while swapping views. |
| **Tier 2 (Inner — AETHER-8)** | `Aether8Root.tsx` header | Toggles AETHER-8's internal drawers and global modes (`HARSH / SOFT SILK`, `OUTPUT MIXER` drawer, `MOD MATRIX` drawer). | **Zero Interruption:** Keeps AETHER-8's `AudioContext`, X0X beat clock, and patch cables running seamlessly. |

